### What problem does this PR solve?

Issue Number: close #28199

Problem Summary: Support schedule state query for placement rules, together with some revisions on the RFC.

### Check List

Tests <!-- At least one of them must be included. -->

- [x] Unit test
- [x] Integration test
- [x] Manual test (add detailed scripts or steps below)

```sh
mycli -h 127.0.0.1 -P 4000 -u root --no-warn << "EOF"
use test;
drop table if exists test.table1;
drop placement policy if exists x;
create placement policy x FOLLOWERS=1;
create table test.table1 (id int primary key) placement policy = "x";
insert into test.table1 values (1);
insert into test.table1 values (2);
insert into test.table1 values (3);
insert into test.table1 values (4);
insert into test.table1 values (5);
show placement;
show placement for database test;
show placement for table table1;
EOF
```

### Release note

<!-- bugfix or new feature needs a release note -->

```release-note
Support query scheduling state using `show placement ...` statements.
```
